# AnyPick rewrites other tools' credential and config files and spawns local
# proxies, so a careless change corrupts a developer's real logins
# (AGENTS.md). Review is not optional here.
#
# Today there is one owner for all of it. This file is still worth having: it
# draws the areas now, so that when a second maintainer arrives the split is a
# decision someone already made rather than one made in a hurry, and so a PR
# that touches the credential boundary is visibly one that needs eyes on it.
#
# This file does not block anything on its own. It only bites once branch
# protection requires a review from code owners — at which point the sole
# maintainer can no longer merge their own PRs, which is the point.

* @outof0

# Credential and config rewriting: a bug here corrupts a real login.
/src/go/internal/client/       @outof0
/src/go/internal/provider/     @outof0
/src/go/internal/activation/   @outof0
/src/go/internal/compensation/ @outof0

# Egress: loopback-only listeners, per-instance secrets, capability pairing
# (ADR 0006, ADR 0016).
/src/go/internal/proxy/        @outof0
/src/go/internal/hub/          @outof0
/src/go/internal/egress/       @outof0
/src/go/internal/transport/    @outof0

# Persistence and the coordinator: the deadlock trap (ADR 0009, ADR 0011).
/src/go/internal/store/        @outof0
/src/go/internal/db/           @outof0
/src/go/internal/journal/      @outof0

# Native apps.
/src/macos/                    @outof0
/src/tauri/                    @outof0

# Gates and authority documents: editing these changes what the repository
# enforces, which is a review decision and not a chore.
/Makefile                      @outof0
/.github/workflows/            @outof0
/adr/                          @outof0
/AGENTS.md                     @outof0
/CODE_REVIEW.md                @outof0
/CONTRIBUTING.md               @outof0
